00:09:04.083 --> 00:09:10.663
The full history since March 2026, including the pre-rules exits, is 98 trades, a 51%

00:09:10.663 --> 00:09:17.063
wind rate with 50 winds, 47 losses, and 1 break even, and cumulative profit and loss of

00:09:17.063 --> 00:09:24.840
minus $18.85. The method is still inside noise, and valuation is the family under test, not a

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:31.120
finished edge. A TFSA holding in a broad market ETF prints a suddenly tight bid-ask on a session

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:36.940
when Chinese state-linked funds in the Bloomberg account report record buying. The machine underneath

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:42.800
is blunt. A government-linked vehicle lifts a huge block of ETF paper in one go, absorbs

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:48.040
the sell side, and the spread you see as a retail order shrinks, while intraday swings calm down.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:52.460
In the most recent week, those funds put up the largest single week total on record,

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:57.500
and the index moved without anyone having to accumulate the underlying name stock by stock.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:02.800
That buffer is why a small limit can fill closer to mid instead of chasing the wide-ask.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:08.160
It is a snowplow clearing the lane, not proof that every driver behind it wanted the road.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:13.000
The habit is to read the prior session's ETF flow in your platform newsfeed before

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.660
the open, which on most Canadian dashboards is under two minutes.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:22.220
If those flows sit above the 20-day average, tighten the limit by one cent and let the extra

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:23.420
liquidity come to you.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:29.060
I have paid the extra spread myself by treating a volume spike as real demand, and that is

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.300
the exact bill this check is meant to avoid.

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:34.800
The misconception is that every burst of size is organic.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:39.620
The fixes to cross-check the flow report before you assume the move survives after the

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.140
coordinated bid steps away.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:45.800
Because when that bid pauses, the spread can gap back out inside a single session.

00:10:46.725 --> 00:10:52.065
Open your screener, filter insurance names for return on equity above 18%, and price

00:10:52.065 --> 00:10:56.505
to book below the five-year median, and write down the top three for review this week.

